Mavergreen's own: llvm-install-name-tool refuses load commands that do not fit, instead of writing them
over the first section.

Why: in a linked image the sections keep their file offsets, and llvm-objcopy's Mach-O layout grows the
load commands in place without checking that they still end before the first section does. An
-add_rpath (or a longer -id or -change) past the header pad overwrote the start of __TEXT,__text and
exited 0, leaving a file llvm-otool and llvm-lipo reject as malformed. ld64.lld's default pad is small
(40 bytes spare on a one-function dylib), so relocating a toolchain-built dylib after the fact hit this;
rust's relocate_prefix did. Apple's install_name_tool refuses the same edit: "larger updated load
commands do not fit (the program must be relinked, and you may need to use -headerpad or
-headerpad_max_install_names)". This makes llvm-install-name-tool (and llvm-objcopy on a linked image)
do the same, naming -headerpad_max_install_names. An edit that still fits, exactly or with room to
spare, is unchanged. Relocatable objects are laid out afresh and are not affected.

A candidate for upstream. tests/headerpad-test.sh is the regression test.

--- a/llvm/lib/ObjCopy/MachO/MachOLayoutBuilder.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/ObjCopy/MachO/MachOLayoutBuilder.cpp
@@ -458,6 +458,25 @@
   constructStringTable();
   updateSymbolIndexes();
   uint64_t Offset = layoutSegments();
+  // A linked image's sections keep their file offsets, so load commands that
+  // grew past the first one would be written over its contents. Refuse, as
+  // Apple's install_name_tool does, rather than emit a corrupt file.
+  if (O.Header.FileType != MachO::HeaderFileType::MH_OBJECT) {
+    const uint64_t HeaderSize =
+        Is64Bit ? sizeof(MachO::mach_header_64) : sizeof(MachO::mach_header);
+    for (const LoadCommand &LC : O.LoadCommands)
+      for (const std::unique_ptr<Section> &Sec : LC.Sections)
+        if (Sec->hasValidOffset() && Sec->Offset != 0 &&
+            Sec->Offset < HeaderSize + O.Header.SizeOfCmds)
+          return createStringError(
+              errc::not_enough_memory,
+              "not enough header space for the updated load commands "
+              "(%u bytes, but section %s,%s starts at offset %u): relink "
+              "with -headerpad_max_install_names",
+              (unsigned)(HeaderSize + O.Header.SizeOfCmds),
+              Sec->Segname.c_str(), Sec->Sectname.c_str(),
+              (unsigned)Sec->Offset);
+  }
   Offset = layoutRelocations(Offset);
   return layoutTail(Offset);
 }
